From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:58:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 19/45] inkling2: sampled streams' drafts race with the
 stream's own keys

The drafter walked greedily at every temperature, so at T 1.0 a draft
landed only when the target's keyed sample happened to be the
drafter's top token. Each walk step of a sampled stream now runs the
same Gumbel race main's sample.cu runs, with the request's seed and
1 / T at the position the draft's token will take. When the two
distributions agree the race lands on the token the verify draws.

The output does not change: the verify still draws its own keyed
sample and keeps a draft only when they are equal. The race ignores
top_k and top_p, which costs some agreement when the request cuts.

Not run on a GPU yet; tf_ink2_race1 has no kernel contract.
